Spec: SpecDD Parser Definition

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Provide minimal IntelliJ PSI parser support for SpecDD language services.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDParserDefinition.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDParserDefinition.kt

Can read:
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/SpecDDLanguageBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Create a PSI lexer that emits one text token over the requested buffer slice.
  Preserve lexer state as 0.
  Preserve lexer buffer sequence and buffer end.
  Advance the PSI lexer to the end of the requested slice.
  Create a parser that consumes all tokens into the requested root node.
  Use a SpecDD file element type backed by `@SpecDDLanguage`.
  Use a text element type backed by `@SpecDDLanguage`.
  Expose empty token sets for whitespace, comments, and string literals.
  Create generic wrapper PSI elements for AST nodes.
  Create `@SpecDDPsiFile` instances for SpecDD file view providers.
  Allow spaces between any tokens.

Must not:
  Implement real SpecDD grammar parsing.
  Implement syntax highlighting tokenization.
  Implement validation diagnostics.
  Classify comments or strings as PSI token sets.
